============
goant is a port of ant to Go.

The engine — lexer, parser, bytecode compiler, interpreter, garbage collector,
the WTF-8 string representation, the NaN-boxed value layout and the 213-opcode
instruction set — is a transliteration of the "Silver" engine in ant
(github.com/theMackabu/ant), a JavaScript runtime written in C. Structures,
opcode semantics and in many places the shape of individual functions follow it
directly; the file comments say where a port diverges and why.

Not a port: the regular-expression engine (see internal/regexp2 below), the
JIT (internal/jitasm, internal/jitmem and internal/engine/jit_*.go — ant's JIT
is built on MIR, and docs/jit-plan.md records why this one is not), and the
embedding API in goant.go and v8go/.
