============
internal/regexp2 is a fork of dlclark/regexp2, itself a port of the .NET regular
expression engine. It carries its own LICENSE and ATTRIB, which cover its
upstreams in turn (dotnet/corefx, the Go standard library, and test data from
the Mono project). The fork exists because ECMAScript and .NET disagree about
nullable loops; internal/regexp2/ATTRIB records what changed.

============
bench/suites/octane holds the Octane 2.0 benchmark suite, fetched rather than
vendored (bench/suites/fetch.sh pins the commit). It carries its own LICENSE and
is not part of the shipped library.

